An addon built against this node is a wasm64 side module that binds its
napi_*, uv_*, v8:: and node:: imports to the node executable that dlopens it,
so its link names that executable as the import provider. It also compiles
with -D__linux__, as node does: uv.h picks uv_loop_t's layout from it, and the
SDK compiler does not define it. The branch keys on target_arch alone, in
target_defaults' OS-independent conditions. node's own build configures
--dest-cpu=x64 and never reaches it. A gyp shared_library (not an addon's
loadable_module) links with --allow-unresolved, ld -shared's default: a name
another dlopen'd module provides reads as a warning.

--- a/common.gypi
+++ b/common.gypi
@@ -448,6 +448,15 @@
       [ 'target_arch=="arm64"', {
         'msvs_configuration_platform': 'arm64',
       }],
+      [ 'target_arch=="wasm64"', {
+        # An addon builds as Linux and links against the node that dlopens it.
+        'defines': [ '__linux__' ],
+        'ldflags': [ '--import-provider=<(node_root_dir)/bin/node' ],
+        # A shared_library leaves undefined names to dlopen, as ld -shared.
+        'target_conditions': [
+          ['_type=="shared_library"', { 'ldflags': [ '--allow-unresolved' ] }],
+        ],
+      }],
